/* 数据管理二级页（整理文件、资源同步、文件已丢失的记录、链接管理、批量删除）:
/* The first-screen skeletons of the data-management second-level pages (organize files, resource sync, records of lost files, link management, bulk delete).
 * Each page is drawn after its own React card: the same Fieldset or data-table frame, the same `max-w-board` content width;
 * titles, descriptions, and headers are static text, written out directly; counts, readouts, library names, and templates wait on the data, so only draw placeholders.
 * The description text shares these constants with the React card; writing two copies would make that section on the skeleton a bit shorter than the real card, and the whole card would jump once on takeover.
 * Result sections that only appear after running a task (scan conclusion, dead-link list) are not pre-drawn. */

/* 量的是 token 对而不是某一条线：`separator-border`:
/* What's measured is a token pair, not a particular line: where `separator-border` draws on which surface is decided by each spot itself;
         the line between the review card's header and the candidate block lands on `primary`, and the footnote strip's line lands on `secondary`. Calling out each one by name
         means adding a new spot requires remembering to add a test case too, and a missing one looks identical on screen to "this spot never had a line".
         Finally, re-check that the divider inside the review card really resolves to this token, so both tiers passing doesn't hide the fact that it never reached the real place. */

/* 输入法正在合成时的按键不归页面：回车在定字，方向键在挑候选字。\n *\n:
/* Key presses while the input method is composing don't belong to the page: Enter is committing the characters, arrow keys are picking a candidate.
 *
 * Checking only `isComposing` isn't enough: Safari also fires a final commit keydown after `compositionend`;
 * on that one `isComposing` is already false and only `keyCode` is still 229, so a form submitted via Enter would get submitted early by it
 * (open-claude-ui `2dc0e988e` fixed exactly this spot). */

/* 页面开着 text-autospace：Chromium 在汉字、假名与拉:
/* The page has text-autospace on: Chromium adds 1/8 em spacing where CJK characters, kana, and Latin letters and digits sit adjacent,
   and full-width punctuation is also squeezed by text-spacing-trim; Canvas measureText accounts for neither. Text containing these characters
   takes the Canvas reading (with estimated spacing added) as its starting point, then confirms each via an offscreen DOM probe; pure Latin text still uses Canvas only. */

